  "completed_components": {
    "G3_complete": "Displayed five-term target regularity bound, with arbitrary theta+eta slack in the excluded-site exponent, and full literal-regime o(1) using Lambda->infinity. Actual private-prime regularity constructs pivots and conditional presence in the original infinite source.",
    "actual_poisson_atoms": "Full target atoms for enumerated distinct-site configurations equal exp(-rate) times the product of signed mark rates. Multiplicities and both signs are retained.",
    "actual_arithmetic_palm": "Presence, exact source masses and true Palm voids are all constructed on the original infinite arithmetic space conditioned on the actual small-prime trace. The source-target mass identity is proved without a mass-factorization premise.",
    "ordinary_deletion": "Countable disjoint source fibres give the original conditional outside-event mass after exact exponential cancellation. The finite full-versus-retained normalized comparison pays the actual outside-start probability and independent target rate.",
    "base_start_avoidance": "The true Palm void equals absence of additional base starts almost surely, using simultaneous run termination preserved by absolute continuity under both conditionings.",
    "normalization_and_G5": "Uniform K=ceil(2*Lambda) penalty <=5*Lambda*p<=M^(-1/2) at the literal source regime. Actual normalized deficit on any retained mask <= the independently proved 7.7 error +M^(-1/2), with explicit baseline inputs. Mean and target-probability completion on changing countable spaces are recorded.",
    "walsh": "Actual finite Walsh coefficients, inversion, mean, exact nonconstant energy and sharp deficit bound; no expansion or variance-identification premise.",
    "affine_environment": "Exact affine indicator and conditional character formulas, unique row multiplier at full row rank, environment law unchanged after planting, and signed conditional Fourier formula retaining the arbitrary environment transform."
  },
  "literature_inputs": "G.3 asymptotic excluded-site counts use baseline PNT. Quantitative G.5 uses the same explicit directional Stein, PNT, Laishram-Shorey and Nicolas-Robin inputs as 7.7. The finite Palm/Poisson masses, deletion, avoidance, normalization, Walsh and affine-environment identities use no literature premise. No proof hole or new axiom. The sequence completion theorem has the actual independently proved 7.7 distance conclusion as its explicit hypothesis, as in the paper corollary.",
  "limits": [
    "G.1–G.3 are proved. G.5 now has the actual arithmetic normalized Palm deficit bound on every retained mask, with the same explicit inputs as 7.7, and its mean/probability completion. G.4 has actual infinite-source mass, avoidance, deletion and finite normalized comparison identities; the exact transfer of the intrinsic G.3 regular set through boundary/start relabelling and restriction still needs to be recorded for its named exceptional probability. G.6 has exact Walsh inversion/energy and the signed affine character formula with an arbitrary environment law; the joint centered-coefficient formula and its complete arithmetic instantiation remain. G.7–G.9 (pair activity, categorical cumulant inequality and arithmetic obstruction), final unnumbered review and separate prescribed-floor full-field specialization remain open. F.2 retains its explicit baseline analytic solution premise.",
    "G.4 has its actual finite identities, but the precise named intrinsic target exception still needs its boundary/start and restriction bridge. G.6 still needs centered-product coefficient assembly and complete arithmetic matrix instantiation.",
    "No new NanoDa/Comparator qualification or Palomar submission for these 794 declarations."
  ],
